{% extends layout %}
{% block page_body %}
	{% set ph_kicker = 'About' %}
	{% set ph_title = 'About ' ~ app_name %}
	{% set ph_lead = 'A learning platform built for organisations that train their own people.' %}
	{% include '@platform/partials/page-head.html.twig' %}
	<section class="container cl-medium py-5">
		<div class="card">
			<div class="card-body">
				<h2>
					What this platform is
				</h2>
				<p>
					{{ app_name }} is a learning-management platform for structured, self-study courses. A course is built from modules, each with its own material and assessment, and a learner works through them at their own pace. Progress, grading, unlocking and certificate eligibility are all decided on the server, so a certificate means what it says.
				</p>
				<p>
					It is built for organisations rather than for individuals alone. A company administrator buys access to a course once and allocates it to staff, sees who has started, who has finished and who has not, and manages their people without needing anybody at {{ app_name }} to do it for them.
				</p>

				<h2>
					How it is built
				</h2>
				<p>
					Server-rendered HTML, enhanced rather than replaced by JavaScript. Every screen works without it: a search is a form, a filter is a link, and a page of results is a page you can bookmark and send to somebody. That is a deliberate choice, not a limitation - a training record that only exists inside a JavaScript application is a training record that can vanish.
				</p>
				<p>
					The platform is themeable. What a theme owns is presentation; what the platform owns is the courses, the rules and the records. A new theme cannot change who may see what.
				</p>

				<h2>
					Who is behind it
				</h2>
				<p>
					{{ app_name }} is designed and built by <strong>Richard Catto</strong>, who owns the product and makes the decisions about where it goes. It is not a re-skinned template or a reseller of somebody else's platform: the courses, the assessment engine, the company model and the theme system are all built here.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you want to talk about using it, or about something it does not yet do, the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> reaches a real person.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
{% endblock %}
